  "review": {
    "en": "Two stories run side by side: a woman who leaves her marriage for love and is shut out by society, and a landowner who searches for a reason to live. Tolstoy renders bodies, rooms, horses and moods with a clarity that hides its own art, and he judges less than his reputation suggests. Few novels hold so much ordinary life.",
    "zh": "两条线并行：一个女人为爱离开婚姻，被上流社会拒之门外；一个地主苦苦寻找活下去的理由。托尔斯泰写身体、房间、马匹和心绪，清晰得让人看不见技巧，评判也比他的名声所暗示的要少。很少有小说装得下这么多寻常生活。"
  },
